{"toolCallId":"call_65110e42427745ac826be4c299fcd8eb","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Four small edits to one bash script: a global, a parser case, a branch inside output_text, and two help blocks. Verification counts lines and diffs the default report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2 or newer, POSIX shell builtins only |\n| **Framework** | None, a single script under the system-spec-kit CLI |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, direct invocation, `wc -l`, `diff` |\n\n### Overview\n\nOne script changes: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. The quiet branch goes inside `output_text()` so the level label keeps one source of truth. You prove it by counting lines in both modes and diffing the default report against a captured baseline.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n- [x] Baseline output captured from the unmodified script\n- [x] Precedence rule for `--json` decided in ADR-001\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] `--quiet` prints one line and the default report matches the baseline byte for byte\n- [ ] Help text and header comment list the flag\n- [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the flag name and the line format\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n\nSingle script branch. The script parses arguments into globals, computes scores, then hands off to one of two renderers: `output_text()` or `output_json()`.\n\n### Key Components\n\n- **Argument parser** (`recommend-level.sh`, section 5): a `case` loop over `$1` that turns flags into globals.\n- **`QUIET` global** (section 2): a boolean beside `JSON_OUTPUT`, read by the renderer.\n- **`output_text()`** (section 4): the text renderer. It owns the `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` string today.\n- **`output_json()`** (section 4): the JSON renderer, unchanged by this work.\n- **Header comment and `show_help()`**: the two places a user reads the option list.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nargv ──► parser ──► LOC, FILES, HAS_*, QUIET, JSON_OUTPUT\n                        │\n                        ▼\n              scores ──► RECOMMENDED_LEVEL, LEVEL_NAME\n                        │\n              ┌─────────┴─────────┐\n              ▼                   ▼\n      output_text()        output_json()\n      QUIET=true?          one JSON document\n      one line : report\n```\n\n### Surfaces Touched\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `output_text()` | Renders the report and the level line | update | `rg -n 'Recommended Level' recommend-level.sh` shows the string in one place |\n| `output_json()` | Renders the JSON document | unchanged | `--json` output diffs empty against the baseline |\n| `show_help()` | Prints the option list | update | `--help` lists `--quiet, -q` |\n| Header comment block | Documents options for a reader of the file | update | `sed -n '1,40p' recommend-level.sh` shows the flag |\n| `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` | Calls the script with `--json` | not a consumer of the text path | `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/commands/speckit/assets/` shows `--json` in both calls |\n| `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-complete.yaml` | Calls the script with `--json` | not a consumer of the text path | same grep |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. The four steps below are the shape of the change.\n\n### Step 1: Initialize the quiet state\n\nAdd `QUIET=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false` in the GLOBALS block. The script runs under `set -euo pipefail`, so a renderer that reads an unset `QUIET` aborts the run instead of printing anything.\n\nAcceptance: `QUIET` is declared before the parser and `bash -n` still exits 0.\nVerify: `rg -n '^QUIET=' recommend-level.sh` prints one line above the parser.\n\n### Step 2: Parse the flag\n\nAdd a `--quiet|-q)` case to the argument loop, setting `QUIET=true` and calling `shift`. Place it beside `--json|-j)` so the two output switches sit together.\n\nAcceptance: both spellings are accepted and neither reaches the unknown-option branch.\nVerify: `bash recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0, and `bash recommend-level.sh -q --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0.\n\n### Step 3: Branch the text renderer\n\nOpen `output_text()` with a quiet guard. When `QUIET` is true, print the level line and return before the blank line, the score row, the breakdown and the phase block.\n\nAcceptance: `--quiet` prints one line, and that line is the one the default report prints.\nVerify: `bash recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n\n### Step 4: Document the flag\n\nAdd `--quiet, -q` to the header OPTIONS block and to `show_help`, with one example that uses it.\n\nAcceptance: both option lists name the flag and at least one example passes it.\nVerify: `bash recommend-level.sh --help | rg -n 'quiet'` prints two lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nNo automated suite covers `recommend-level.sh` today. The verification is a set of commands a reader can rerun, captured in `tasks.md`.\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Syntax | The edited script parses | `bash -n` |\n| Output parity | Quiet line equals the report line | `diff <(quiet run) <(default run | sed -n '2p')` |\n| Regression | Default report matches the pre-change baseline | `diff` against `scratch/baseline-default.txt` |\n| Exit codes and stderr | Invalid input in both modes | `bash recommend-level.sh --loc abc` with `$?` |\n| Help | Option list names the flag | `--help` piped to `rg` |\n\nThe baseline files live in `scratch/` and are captured from the unmodified script before the first edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2 or newer | Internal | Green | The script cannot run |\n| `diff`, `wc`, `rg` for verification | Internal | Green | Verify by reading the output instead |\n| The unmodified script for a baseline | Internal | Green | Capture the baseline from `git stash` or a copy before editing |\n\nNo new package, library or service is required.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes for any argument set, or a caller that passes `--json` sees different output.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`, then rerun the two baseline diffs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Implementation | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 20 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **1 hour (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] Baseline output captured (no data to back up)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured (not applicable, the flag is the switch)\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set (not applicable, a local CLI script)\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that edits `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Run `bash -n` on the restored file.\n3. Rerun the default and `--json` diffs against `scratch/baseline-default.txt` and `scratch/baseline-json.json`.\n4. Tell the callers who adopted `--quiet` that the flag is gone.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A, the script keeps no state\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐\n│  Phase 1     │────►│  Phase 2         │────►│  Phase 3       │\n│  Setup       │     │  Implementation  │     │  Verification  │\n└──────────────┘     └──────────────────┘     └────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | `scratch/baseline-*.txt` | Verification |\n| `QUIET` global | None | A readable boolean | Parser case, quiet branch |\n| Parser case | `QUIET` global | `QUIET=true` on demand | Quiet branch |\n| Quiet branch in `output_text()` | Parser case | The one-line output | Verification |\n| Help blocks | Flag name | Option list and examples | Documentation checks |\n| Verification | All of the above | Command evidence | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the baseline** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Add the global and the parser case** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Add the quiet branch** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n4. **Verify both modes** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: 1 hour\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- The two help blocks can be edited while the verification baseline runs.\n- `spec.md` wording and the help text can be reviewed in the same pass, since both name the flag.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline-default.txt` holds 16 lines | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag parsed | `--quiet` and `-q` both exit 0 | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | One-line output | `--quiet ... | wc -l` prints 1 | Phase 2 |\n| M4 | Release ready | Both diffs empty and `bash -n` exits 0 | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: `--json` takes precedence over `--quiet`\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script has one output switch today, `--json`. A quiet mode adds a second one that also decides what stdout holds. Passing both asks for a text line and a JSON document at once, and the script has to pick one.\n\n**Decision**: `--json` wins. When both flags are present the script prints the JSON document and adds no text line. The quiet branch sits inside `output_text()`, which `--json` never reaches, so the precedence falls out of the existing structure and needs no new code.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- A caller that wants a single text line never passes `--json`, and a caller that passes `--json` gets a single machine-readable document either way.\n- `--quiet --json` silently drops the quiet request. Mitigation: the help text and REQ-009 state the precedence, and a caller who needs both reads one JSON field instead.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error out when both flags are passed: adds an error path and a new exit code for a combination that already has a sensible answer.\n- Let `--quiet` win and print the text line: a caller that asked for JSON would get text, which is the more surprising of the two outcomes.\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":136,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":105}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
